                        "entry_id": "7429e44c-7c85-35a5-bf67-b12b5508adad",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The lack, absence, or antithesis of grace; gracelessness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "683c14d0-7b5f-4cae-8b46-fedf3276131e",
                                "sense_id": "4f5bf989-7ba2-31f2-a8e0-344697c59b26",
                                "text": "The evil ungraces of the wicked Devil are thus called in Latin speech: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a171c2b0-fe6f-4571-8682-0c5863ec2c18",
                                "sense_id": "4f5bf989-7ba2-31f2-a8e0-344697c59b26",
                                "text": "However, as costly as grace is, ungrace costs more."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac4c5056-1f74-4ab3-8054-a97c0632cc69",
                                "sense_id": "4f5bf989-7ba2-31f2-a8e0-344697c59b26",
                                "text": "There is the contract between ungrace religion and a spirituality that is grace and compassion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8c0c9ea-712d-44ba-9660-cec151852a41",
                                "sense_id": "4f5bf989-7ba2-31f2-a8e0-344697c59b26",
                                "text": "Every institution, it seems, runs on ungrace and its insistence that we earn our way."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
